OF THE USER</strong> <br> <br> <br> <strong>2.1. Non-commercial Use</strong><br> <br> The USER receives wireless internet access services related to Türk Telekom WIFI. The rights that are granted by Türk Telekom to the USER in relation to Türk Telekom WIFI are only for non-commercial and personal use of Türk Telekom WIFI. The USER cannot, either directly or indirectly, acquire any revenues or similar benefits from the use of Türk Telekom WIFI. <br> <br> The USER can learn the scope of the rights concerning the use of Türk Telekom WIFI service pack on Türk Telekom’s websites at <a href="http://www.turktelekomwifi.com" target="_blank" style="background: #FFFFFF; color: #1ba3ac; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;">www.turktelekomwifi.com</a> or <a href="http://www.turktelekom.com.tr" target="_blank" style="background: #FFFFFF; color: #1ba3ac; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;">www.turktelekom.com.tr</a> any other website to be designated by OPERATOR. By accepting this AGREEMENT, the USER agrees to the scope of rights concerning use of this pack. Therefore, please access the information regarding the packs via the above-mentioned websites, and read them carefully. OPERATOR reserves the right to make amendments to the rights that are granted to the USER within the scope of subscription at any time. The USER cannot, in any manner whatsoever, make any interventions and actions which may cause damage or prevent access to, overload or impair the websites, goods and services, software or data of OPERATOR, or those of its content, medium or platform providers, and cannot use Türk Telekom WIFI in such manner or in a manner that may prevent third parties from utilizing OPERATOR’s services. <br> <br> The USER can by no means transfer, lease, sell its rights under this AGREEMENT, or offer them to the use and/or benefit of third parties, even for free of charge, without obtaining the written consent of OPERATOR. Use of Türk Telekom WIFI shall always be subject to the terms of this AGREEMENT. <br> <br> <br> <strong>2.2. Appropriate Use</strong><br> <br> The USER accepts that he/she will use Türk Telekom WIFI in compliance with all applicable national and international legislation, rules and laws regarding public order and morality and use of internet, and show respect to the rights of third parties. The responsibility for any acts of detection, tapping of the communication, assessment and recording of the signal data that will be conducted within the scope of duties and powers of the Chairmanship of Telecommunication and Communication of the Information Technologies and Communication Authority, and the responsibility for use in compliance with the Law numbered 5651 regarding the Regulation of Publications Made on Internet and Combat against the Crimes Committed via These Publications and other Laws, and the Regulation Concerning Principles and Procedures for Regulating the Publications Made through Internet and other relevant regulations shall be borne exclusively by the USER. The USER may not use Türk Telekom WIFI in violation of law, contrary to its purposes of use, fraudulently or for inappropriate purposes, may not give permission to third parties to act as such, or participate in or encourage performance of such acts, may not act in violation of this AGREEMENT, as may be amended from time to time, may not allow third parties to exercise the rights acquired under this AGREEMENT, and may not allow or encourage any third parties to conduct such acts. In the event of any such acts performed by the USER, OPERATOR may terminate this AGREEMENT. In such case, all the other legal rights of OPERATOR shall be reserved. <br> <br> The USER accepts that the system settings ascertained by OPERATOR shall be valid. The USER shall be responsible for any problems and issues arising from the USER and the devices under his/her responsibility, and OPERATOR may not be held responsible for any faults in this respect. The USER shall, in order to be able use the Türk Telekom WIFI service, be obligated to provide a computer which is suitable for internet connection and a suitable mobile device. The responsibility for providing the necessary security measures such as firewalls and anti-virus protection in order to prevent any damages that may occur during Türk Telekom WIFI connection shall belong to the USER. <br> <br> The responsibility for the security and use of the usernames and passwords which have been allocated to the USER for use of the services provided by OPERATOR shall belong to the USER. In case the usernames and passwords are lost or stolen, the USER must promptly notify OPERATOR in order that these usernames and passwords can be changed. Administrative, legal, financial and penal liabilities which may arise from unauthorized use of passwords shall belong to the USER. <br> <br> The USER is obligated to ensure that “all the usernames and other names” that he/she uploads to the system in relation to the services it receives do not infringe third parties’ legal rights such as copyrights, trademarks, commercial titles and business enterprise names. If the USER violates the provisions of this article, OPERATOR shall be entitled to request the USER to eliminate such violation of the AGREEMENT or to cancel the subscription of the USER, either on a temporary or permanent basis, without serving prior notice to the USER. If “all the usernames and other names” uploaded by the USER to the system” violate the intellectual and property rights of third parties, including copyrights, trademarks, commercial titles or business enterprise names, the responsibility for any third party claims that may arise shall be borne solely by the USER. The USER shall defend, promptly indemnify and hold OPERATOR harmless against any such claims. You can visit <a href="http://www.turktelekom.com.tr" target="_blank" style="background: #FFFFFF; color: #1ba3ac; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;">www.turktelekom.com.tr</a> or call 444 1 444 Türk Telekom Customer Service Line for any queries and problems regarding Türk Telekom WIFI. <br> <br> <br> <strong>2.3. Financial Liabilities</strong><br> <br> The fees in respect of the Türk Telekom WIFI service that will be provided to the USER shall be specified at <a href="http://www.turktelekomwifi.com" target="_blank" style="background: #FFFFFF; color: #1ba3ac; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;">www.turktelekomwifi.com</a> or <a href="http://www.turktelekom.com.tr" target="_blank" style="background: #FFFFFF; color: #1ba3ac; font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 13px;">www.turktelekom.com.tr</a> By accepting this AGREEMENT, the USER agrees to pay the fees for the Türk Telekom WIFI service either by credit card or by any other means of payment. The USER shall be responsible for the accuracy of the information which he/she provides as to the elected method of payment. In the event of any delay in the payment of the Türk Telekom WIFI service fees, default interest shall be applied to the relevant fees. <br> <br> <br> <strong>3. RIGHTS AND LIABILITIES OF OPERATOR</strong><br> <br> OPERATOR shall be free to use any and all technologies it may deem appropriate for provision of WIFI services within the framework of designated practices and service requirements, and to change, at any time, the technology being used. OPERATOR is entitled to enter into agreements with any third persons or companies for any of its liabilities, and to have the operation and maintenance of Türk Telekom WIFI service carried out by others either in part or in whole.<br> <br> OPERATOR may give “links” to other web sites and/or portals, files or contents which are owned, and operated by third party vendors, providers and other third parties which are not under its control. These “links” might have been provided by OPERATOR for ease of reference only, and do not intend to support the web site