isclosed, displayed, edited, cannot be reverse engineered, recompiled, source code created or used in any other way in whole or in part, whether for commercial purposes or not.",per_data_p2:"All trademarks and logos on this website are owned by Türk Telekom or relevant third parties. Such trademarks and logos may never be used, permanently downloaded, copied or distributed without the written consent of their respective owners.",per_data_no_1:"Visitors to the site have the right to use the site only to access the website or to use services provided in accordance with the terms of use and legal limits and only in a way to be limited with the above-mentioned purposes. Such a right to use cannot be interpreted as Türk Telekom granting the visitors a right of license.",per_data_no_1_p1:"Investor relations and annual and temporary reports, general views, presentations, audio and video files (live or recorded) related to activities, which are present on this website, and other documents on this website shall include forward-looking statements and remarks made by Türk Telekom. Forward-looking statements on the website, such as “anticipa␀��␀␀te,” “believe,” “estimate,” “hope,” “plan,” and “design”, shall reflect Türk Telekom’s forward-looking views at the time of the statement. Changes in general economic and commercial conditions, the introduction of competing or new products and services, and changes in business strategic decisions may result in actual results differing significantly from those anticipated here. Türk Telekom is under no obligation to update these statements, which include forecasts and terms for the future.",per_data_no_1_p2:"Türk Telekom makes no promises, guarantees, or verifications about the accuracy, reliability, completeness, validity or appropriateness of the information provided on this website. Türk Telekom assumes no responsibility for any errors in the information provided on the website.",per_data_no_1_p3:"This website owned by Türk Telekom may contain links to other websites for the convenience of its users. Such websites are not reviewed by Türk Telekom and are owned by third parties who are not directly or indirectly under Türk Telekom’s control and/or authority. When the third-party websites are accessed, the rules and data protection policies of those websites should be reviewed.",per_data_no_1_p4:"Links provided by Türk Telekom to such third-party websites cannot be interpreted as an endorsement of that website or products or services stated on the third-party website.",per_data_no_1_p5:"Türk Telekom does not explicitly or implicitly endorse the contents of the websites to which it links or other links given in such websites, and is not responsible for such contents or links. The user solely bears all risk and responsibility arising from the use of such third-party websites.",per_data_no_1_p6:"The data collected while visiting the website shall be recorded and processed in accordance with the data security rules in effect. Türk Telekom cannot be held responsible for the data privacy practices of third-party links on the website.",per_data_no_2:"The IP address of the visitor provided by the internet service provider, the website found before accessing the website, the pages visited through the website, date and duration of the visit shall be recorded as standard by the servers when the website is visited. Personal data shall only be recorded if entered by the visitor.",per_data_no_2_l1:"The data collected on the website shall be processed in connection with the services provided and used for purposes such as technical administration of the website, customer management, product surveys, marketing, notifying changes on the website, new services or offers, and so on.",per_data_no_2_l2:"Türk Telekom shall act diligently to ensure that its employees and distributors comply with the confidentiality principle. However, the data may be shared with Türk Telekom’s partners or upon the requests from authorized public authorities, which must be disclosed to authorities expressly authorized legally as per applicable legal regulations, finalized court decisions, or administrative orders.",per_data_no_2_l3:"Türk Telekom shall employ technical and organizational security measures to prevent the data it manages from being altered, lost, damaged, or used by unauthorized persons, and shall take precautions to protect personal data.",per_data_no_2_l4:"PERSONAL DATA PROTECTION ",per_data_no_2_l5:"TTNET accepts, declares, and agrees to abide by all regulations, procedures and principles in force regarding the protection of Personal Data, in particular the Law on the Protection of Personal Data No. 6698 (“KVKK”), the Electronic Communications Law No. 5809 and its secondary regulations, and Board decisions and guidelines (“Data Protection Legislation”). TTNET accepts, declares, and agrees that all of its activities related to the processing of personal data obtained from the User or received on behalf of the other party during the performance of the Agreement are subject to any applicable or future national legislation regarding the protection of personal data, specifically Law on the Protection of Personal Data, and compliance with this legislation in all transaction processes involving personal data is covered in its legal obligations. In addition, it agrees, declares and undertakes that it shall also comply with the principles set forth in the Board Decisions and Guidelines to be published by the Personal Data Protection Board ('Board') within the scope of personal data legislation. ",per_data_no_2_l6:"To the extent which is necessary for TTNET to provide services, the User consents to the collection, processing and use of their Personal Data for the purposes of performance measurement / rating, business development, and communication activities, statistical, administrative and accounting purposes, in order to adapt TTNET’s offer to the expectations of the User, to increase the quality of services, to create a collective image for Users and to advertise. ",per_data_no_2_l7:"TTNET shall be able to transfer it to a third party or organization or Group Companies under the same conditions, in accordance with the KVKK and Data Protection Legislation, for the purposes specified in the “Clarification Text”. User accepts that his/her personal information can be stored and processed in organizations or in the country with which TTNET has contracted, for the purposes set forth in this Agreement, in accordance with the KVKK and Data Protection Legislation. ",per_data_no_2_l8:"All these Personal Data belonging to User shall be processed, stored and used for the purposes specified in the Clarification Text in accordance with the KVKK, the Data Protection Legislation and, in any case, the Clarification Text on the TTNET's Website. ",per_data_no_2_l9:"Türk Telekom website can always be visited free of charge. Personal information such as name and surname, postal address, date of birth, gender, telephone and fax number, e-mail address, subscription transactions for a service offered by our Company shall only be obtained by Türk Telekom only with the consent and knowledge of the visitor, and may not be disclosed to third parties unless the person sharing the information expressly consents to it. Türk Telekom cannot be held responsible for any errors or omissions in the content, or for any incorrect information submitted by the visitor, including, but not limited to, any possible loss or damage resulting from the use of the content of the website.",per_data_no_2_l10:"Türk Telekom and/or its employees shall not be responsible for any loss or damage, even if they were advised of the possibility of the loss or damage including, but not limited to, direct or indirect damages and expenses arising as a result of performance failure, error, deficiency, interruption, defect, operation and/or transmission delay, computer virus and/or line and/or system failure that may occur during or after using the website.",per_data_no_2_l11:"Türk Telekom reserves the right, without prior notice, to change all products and services, pages, information, visual items, and content on this website.",per_data_no_2_l12:"If personal data entry is requested from you on Türk Telekom website, your personal information (name, surname, address, Republic of Turkey ID No, date of birth, e-mail, phone, fax, demographic information or customer ID, etc.) shall be used by Türk Telekom only for sending you information messages",per_data_no_2_l13:"and shall never be disclosed to third parties except for legal obligations or as per your permission.",per_data_no_2_l14:"If you do not want to receive direct marketing messages from Türk Telekom, please let us know by clicking the “unregister” link at the bottom of each message you receive, or by contacting us using our contact information."},cookie_policy:{header:"TÜRK TELEKOMÜNİKASYON AŞ.",header_2:"COOKIES POLICY",per_data_p1:"As Türk Telekomünikasyon A.Ş. and its Group Companies, we use cookies on our web pages. Regarding the cookies used on these websites, each Türk Telekom Group Company act as separate data controllers pursuant to the Law on the Protection of Personal Data No. 6698. By using our web pages, you consent to the use of these cookies in line with the remarks below and your preferences.",per_data_p2:"Our cookie policy that you are reading contains information about the cookies, how we use them and how you can change your preferences for such cookies.",per_data_no_1:"What are cookies?",per_data_no_1_p1:"Cookies are small text files that the web pages you visit send to you through your internet browser. Cookies files are stored in your web browser and identifies you, thus facilitating your next visit and making the web service more convenient this way. Cookies can be stored for the duration of a web session (session cookies), whereas there are also cookies stored for a longer but limited period of time 